<section class="page-head">
  <p class="kicker">The Workshop</p>
  <h1>Products</h1>
  <p class="lede muted">Instruments of the order — printed, turned, bound, stitched, cast and posted.
  Attire, jewellery, press and sundries, under four marks drawn for the purpose.</p>
</section>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal" id="marks">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">The Marks</p>
    <h2>Four Logos, and What Each One Argues</h2>
    <p class="muted">A mark is a compressed argument. These four are drawn as vector art — they are
    live SVG on this page, not pictures of logos — so they go on a seal, a hoodie or a billboard
    without losing a hairline.</p>

    <div class="mark-grid">
      <figure class="mark">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="The Mirrored Tree: a tree whose roots repeat its branches inside a double ring of eleven markers">
          <circle cx="60" cy="60" r="55" fill="none" stroke="#d7b05a" stroke-width="1"/>
          <circle cx="60" cy="60" r="51" fill="none" stroke="#d7b05a" stroke-width="0.5"/>
          {%- for i in range(0, 11) %}
          <circle cx="{{ (60 + 53 * ((6.2832 * i / 11) | sin)) | round2 }}"
                  cy="{{ (60 - 53 * ((6.2832 * i / 11) | cos)) | round2 }}" r="1.7" fill="#d7b05a"/>
          {%- endfor %}
          <path d="M60 58 V36 M60 46 L48 34 M60 46 L72 34 M60 38 L52 28 M60 38 L68 28"
                stroke="#f3ddaa" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          <path d="M60 62 V84 M60 74 L48 86 M60 74 L72 86 M60 82 L52 92 M60 82 L68 92"
                stroke="#7fae7a" stroke-width="1.6" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          <circle cx="60" cy="60" r="3.2" fill="none" stroke="#d7b05a" stroke-width="1.2"/>
          <path d="M60 18 l1.8 4.4 4.7.4-3.6 3.1 1.1 4.6L60 28l-4 2.1 1.1-4.6-3.6-3.1 4.7-.4z" fill="#f3ddaa"/>
        </svg>
        <figcaption><strong>The Mirrored Tree.</strong> Roots repeating branches: the claim that the
        pattern below ground and the pattern above it are one pattern. Eleven markers on the rim, one
        star over the crown for the thing still unaccounted for.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="mark">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="The Open Question: a vertical stave crossed by three bars inside a ring">
          <circle cx="60" cy="60" r="48" fill="none" stroke="#d7b05a" stroke-width="1.4"/>
          <path d="M60 20 V100" stroke="#f3ddaa" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          <path d="M40 42 H80 M34 60 H86 M40 78 H80" stroke="#d7b05a" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
          <circle cx="60" cy="60" r="7" fill="#0e0c0a" stroke="#7fae7a" stroke-width="1.4"/>
        </svg>
        <figcaption><strong>The Open Question.</strong> One stave for the enquiry, three bars for
        evidence, history and experience, and a gap at the crossing that is deliberately not filled in.
        It is the order&rsquo;s seal because it refuses to be an answer.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="mark">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="The Eleven Limbs: eleven rays from a central eye">
          <circle cx="60" cy="60" r="50" fill="none" stroke="#d7b05a" stroke-width="1"/>
          {%- for i in range(0, 11) %}
          <line x1="{{ (60 + 14 * ((6.2832 * i / 11) | sin)) | round2 }}"
                y1="{{ (60 - 14 * ((6.2832 * i / 11) | cos)) | round2 }}"
                x2="{{ (60 + 49 * ((6.2832 * i / 11) | sin)) | round2 }}"
                y2="{{ (60 - 49 * ((6.2832 * i / 11) | cos)) | round2 }}"
                stroke="#d7b05a" stroke-width="{% if i == 0 %}2.2{% else %}1{% endif %}"/>
          {%- endfor %}
          <ellipse cx="60" cy="60" rx="13" ry="8" fill="none" stroke="#f3ddaa" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <circle cx="60" cy="60" r="3.4" fill="#7fae7a"/>
        </svg>
        <figcaption><strong>The Eleven Limbs.</strong> One ray per limb, all of them leaving the same
        eye. The heavy ray is whichever limb you are standing in; it is drawn thicker because nobody
        studies all eleven at once and pretending otherwise is a lie.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="mark">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 120 120" role="img" aria-label="The Aether Knot: a looped band with a half twist">
          <path d="M30 60 C30 32 90 32 90 60 C90 88 30 88 30 60 Z" fill="none" stroke="#d7b05a" stroke-width="2"/>
          <path d="M30 60 C30 44 90 76 90 60" fill="none" stroke="#8fb6d8" stroke-width="1.6"/>
          <path d="M30 60 C30 76 90 44 90 60" fill="none" stroke="#c98b6a" stroke-width="1.6"/>
          <circle cx="60" cy="60" r="2.6" fill="#f3ddaa"/>
          <circle cx="60" cy="60" r="52" fill="none" stroke="#d7b05a" stroke-width="0.6"/>
        </svg>
        <figcaption><strong>The Aether Knot.</strong> A band given a half twist before its ends were
        joined: one side, one edge, no inside. The field under everything, drawn as the one shape that
        cannot be told apart from its own reverse.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">&#10022;</div>

<section class="wrap narrow reveal">
  <div class="frame">
    <p class="kicker">The Lines We Print</p>
    <ul class="quote-list">
      <li>&ldquo;Life, Love, Magic.&rdquo;<span>the creed, and the only three words on the plain goods</span></li>
      <li>&ldquo;Test everything kindly.&rdquo;<span>the house rule, and the mug</span></li>
      <li>&ldquo;An order of enquiry.&rdquo;<span>the tote, the letterhead, the gate</span></li>
      <li>&ldquo;Name the thing accurately. That is the first act of magic.&rdquo;<span>the codex, page one</span></li>
      <li>&ldquo;The aether was never disproved. One clause of it was struck out.&rdquo;<span>the physics print</span></li>
      <li>&ldquo;Four instruments, one sky.&rdquo;<span>the astrolabe engraving</span></li>
      <li>&ldquo;An answer that cannot survive your scepticism has not earned your belief.&rdquo;<span>the reading-room poster</span></li>
      <li>&ldquo;Roots repeat branches.&rdquo;<span>inside the collar of every garment</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted xsmall">Every line above is the order&rsquo;s own, taken from its pages rather than
    bought in. Nothing here quotes a living person without saying so.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="divider">&#10022;</div>

<section class="wrap">
  <div class="grid three">
    {% for p in products %}
    <article class="frame card product reveal">
      <figure><img src="{{ p.img }}" alt="{{ p.name }}" loading="lazy" width="800" height="600"></figure>
      <p class="tag">{{ p.group or "The Press" }} · {{ p.kind }}</p>
      <h3>{{ p.name }}</h3>
      <p>{{ p.desc }}</p>
      <p class="price">{{ p.price }}</p>
      <p><a class="btn" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}?subject=Order:%20{{ p.name | urlencode }}">Enquire / Order</a></p>
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>

  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <div class="upload-note">
      <strong>For Ed — the shop.</strong> Items live in <code>src/_data/products.json</code>. To take real
      payments without running a server, swap the <em>Enquire</em> link for a Stripe Payment Link, a Gumroad
      button or a Shopify Buy Button — all three are a single URL and work on a static site. Product photography
      goes in <code>src/assets/img/</code>.
    </div>
    <div class="frame mt-2">
      <h3>Shipping &amp; Ethics</h3>
      <p class="muted">Printed on FSC stock with vegetable inks; wooden items turned from windfall and
      coppice timber. Nothing in this shop promises to heal, cure or protect you. They are beautiful objects
      for thinking with, sold as exactly that.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
